HAVEN: Pet Emergency Response System
Product Requirements Document (PRD)

Product Overview
HAVEN is an integrated mobile and desktop emergency response system designed specifically for pet-related emergencies. The system connects pet owners to local emergency response units, veterinarians, and animal rescue organizations in real time.
It consists of two main components:
Mobile Application (User Side): Used by pet owners to send one-click emergency alerts or detailed incident reports.


Desktop Application (Response Unit Side): Used by emergency response teams, animal welfare officers, and partnered veterinarians to receive, track, and respond to alerts.


HAVEN aims to provide faster, more coordinated, and transparent pet emergency responses across communities.

Core Concept
When a pet owner encounters an emergency (such as injury, heatstroke, animal attack, or distress), they can press the big red emergency button on the HAVEN mobile app. This immediately sends a real-time alert to the emergency response unit’s desktop dashboard, pinpointing the user’s location and contact details.
Responders can then:
View the alert on a live interactive map, represented as a pulsing red dot.


Access the pet owner’s profile for quick contact and verification.


Dispatch field responders or coordinate with nearby veterinary clinics.


The system also includes an emergency form for non-critical incidents (e.g., lost pets, minor injuries, or animal rescues), and a live map accessible to users for awareness of ongoing pet emergencies within their vicinity.

Target Users
Pet owners and animal caregivers


Veterinary clinics and hospitals


Animal control and rescue units


Local barangay animal response teams


Pet welfare NGOs and government animal bureaus



Objectives
Create a centralized and digital emergency response network for pets.


Minimize response time by automating alerts with precise GPS data.


Provide real-time situational awareness through mapping and alert visualization.


Establish data-driven insights for future pet welfare and safety initiatives.



Key Features
Mobile Application (User Side)
Account Creation and Verification: Users register with contact details, pet information, and address.


One-Tap Emergency Button: Instantly alerts the emergency response unit with real-time GPS coordinates.


Emergency Form Submission: Allows users to file detailed reports for non-critical incidents.


Live Map View: Displays ongoing emergency activity and nearby rescue operations.


Notification System: Provides updates when responders are dispatched or arrive on-site.


Desktop Application (Response Unit Side)
Real-Time Live Map Dashboard: Displays pulsing red dots for reported emergencies within the unit’s area of responsibility.


User Profiling Page: Stores data of registered pet owners, including contact and emergency history.


Incident Log System: Automatically records all emergency reports for documentation and analytics.


Response Monitoring Dashboard: Shows statistics such as response times, case frequency, and resolved cases.


Communication Interface: Enables responders to contact the reporting pet owner directly via integrated call or message functions.



System Flow
The user presses the emergency button, sending an alert with location and contact details.


The response unit dashboard updates in real time, showing a pulsing red dot on the map.


Responders assess the case and contact the pet owner for details.


A veterinarian or rescue team is dispatched.


The incident is automatically logged into the database for review and analytics.



Technical Specifications
Mobile Application (Prototype)
Framework: React Native (via Expo Go)


Development Tools: Expo CLI, Visual Studio Code


API Communication: RESTful APIs for sending alerts and retrieving data


Map Integration: Google Maps API / Mapbox


Data Storage: Firebase Firestore (real-time database)


Authentication: Firebase Auth (Email and Phone Sign-in)


Testing Environment: Expo Go (Android/iOS mobile testing)


Desktop Application (Prototype)
Framework: Java Swing (for UI)


Programming Language: Java SE 17


Database: MySQL / Firebase Realtime Database (for prototype sync)


Mapping Integration: Embedded web view (Google Maps API)


Backend Server (optional): Node.js or Java Servlet for API endpoints


Data Communication: JSON-based REST API between desktop and mobile systems



System Architecture
Client Side (Mobile App):
 Sends emergency alerts, receives response updates, and displays map data.
Server Layer:
 Handles requests, authentication, and real-time event updates.
Admin Side (Desktop App):
 Receives alerts, updates dashboards, and logs data for analytics.
All components are connected through a cloud-based database (Firebase), ensuring synchronization and real-time updates across devices.

Data Privacy and Security
All user data (contact details, pet information, and GPS coordinates) are encrypted during transmission.


Authentication ensures only verified users can send or view emergency data.


Role-based access control limits sensitive data exposure.



Project Tools and Environment
